# Environments
# A backup or variant of .env holds the same live keys as .env itself, and the
# bare `.env` line matches exactly one filename. `.env*` covers every suffix
# shape — `.env.bak.1234`, `.env.local`, `.env_backup`, `.env.save` — including
# the ones with no dot after `env`, which `.env.*` silently missed. `*.env`
# additionally covers the prefixed form (`prod.env`). `!.env.example` must stay
# BELOW both, since a later pattern wins: it re-admits the committed template,
# which holds placeholders and no secrets. Being un-anchored, it re-admits
# `frontend/.env.example` too.
.env*
*.env
!.env.example
.envrc
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

